SET biography = $$Lazzarini & Pickering is a Rome-based architecture and design studio founded in 1982 by Claudio Lazzarini (Rome, 1953) and Carl Pickering (Sydney, 1960), who met while studying at the Università La Sapienza in Rome. Over four decades the practice has built a reputation for an architecture of restraint and luminous precision — work that distils Mediterranean light, classical proportion and Milanese rigour into spaces of quiet, almost cinematic clarity.

Their portfolio moves fluently between private residences, yachts, retail interiors, exhibition design and furniture, and includes long-standing collaborations with Fendi, Bulgari, Versace and Genny, as well as award-winning houses across Italy, the Côte d'Azur and the eastern Mediterranean. Whether reconfiguring a palazzo in Rome or detailing the interior of a sailing yacht, the studio works as a single hand: walls slide, volumes rotate, and storage dissolves into joinery so that the inhabited space remains pure geometry inflected by light.

Their long-standing partnership with Marta Sala Éditions has produced some of the most refined Italian collectible furniture of the last decade — pieces rooted in the Milanese design ethos and Bauhaus-inspired rigour, yet softened by a Roman feeling for surface and patina. Materials are chosen for the way they age: hand-rubbed bronze, smoked oak, parchment, vellum, hand-stitched leather, travertine and Calacatta marble are detailed with the tolerances of a cabinetmaker rather than an industrial producer.

Recipients of the Compasso d'Oro selection, the Dedalo Minosse International Prize and multiple Wallpaper* Design Awards, Lazzarini and Pickering have exhibited at the Venice Biennale and the Triennale di Milano, and their work is regularly published in Domus, AD, Wallpaper* and The World of Interiors. The studio remains deliberately small, with Claudio and Carl personally directing every project — an approach that places them firmly within the lineage of European architect-designers for whom interior, object and architecture are a single, continuous discipline.$$
WHERE slug = 'lazzarini-pickering';